  },
  "question": {
    "text": "To light, a <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">W</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> lamp is connected, in series with a capacitor of capacitance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>50</mn><mrow><mi>&#960;</mi><msqrt><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">x</mi></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#956;</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">F</mi></math>, with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>Hz</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>AC</mi></math> source. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> will be _____ ."
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "3",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Electrical power is given by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>R</mi></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi>P</mi></mfrac></math></p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0069_21bac3765056.png\" style=\"width: 170px; height: 249px;\" /></p><p>Resistance of lamp is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn></mrow><mn>50</mn></mfrac><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi></math></p></blockquote><blockquote><p>Let&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi></msub></math>&nbsp;be the voltage across capacitor and resistor.</p><p>Here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>V</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p>Current through lamp is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>100</mn><mn>200</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>100</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mn>200</mn></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mn>30000</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msub><mi>V</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>100</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math></p><p>We know that,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>V</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>&#160;</mo></math></p><p>Then,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>C</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>200</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#937;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>&#969;C</mi></mfrac></math></p><p>So, capacitance of capacitor is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>20</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>20</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msqrt><mi>x</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>50</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>100</mn><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>200</mn><msqrt><mn>3</mn></msqrt></math></p><p>Thus, value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>"
  }
}